89.4" cy="78" r="6" data-pf="c-ffffff" data-ps="c-5f6f2a" stroke-width="2.2"/><circle cx="296.6" cy="78" r="6.5" data-pf="c-5f6f2a"/><text x="466" y="83" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-weight="600" data-pf="c-2e6a2b">63%</text><text x="0" y="116" font-size="12.5" data-pf="c-141414">3.4–3.6 mm</text><path d="M236.3 112H310.0" data-ps="c-5f6f2a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="236.3" cy="112" r="6" data-pf="c-ffffff" data-ps="c-5f6f2a" stroke-width="2.2"/><circle cx="310.0" cy="112" r="6.5" data-pf="c-5f6f2a"/><text x="466" y="117" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-weight="600" data-pf="c-2e6a2b">69%</text><text x="0" y="150" font-size="12.5" data-pf="c-141414">3.6–3.8 mm</text><path d="M248.1 146H356.9" data-ps="c-5f6f2a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="248.1" cy="146" r="6" data-pf="c-ffffff" data-ps="c-5f6f2a" stroke-width="2.2"/><circle cx="356.9" cy="146" r="6.5" data-pf="c-5f6f2a"/><text x="466" y="151" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" font-weight="600" data-pf="c-2e6a2b">69%</text></svg>
          <figcaption class="caption">Mean grain size of four bud sizes, hollow on day 0 and filled on day 5, with the share over 30 µm that day (the thesis, pp. 27–28).</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>Buds of 3 to 3.4 mm proved best; viability fell over the week, so the culture still needs work.</p>
